.TH AD_LAYER_REORDER 1 "2026-08-30" "ad 2.0" "ad layers"
.SH NAME
ad_layer_reorder \- 4-sweep reorder layer (normalize op order and positions)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_layer_reorder
< raw_ops > reordered_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_layer_reorder
is the first layer in the postprocess pipeline. It takes raw char ops from
.BR ad_compute (1)
and reorders them for human readability using a 4-sweep algorithm, then sets per-op (line, col) positions.
.PP
The 4 sweeps within each change region (consecutive non-keep, non-\\n ops):
.RS
.IP 1. 3
Non-newline DELETE ops (content being removed on this line)
.IP 2. 3
Non-newline INSERT ops (content being added on this line)
.IP 3. 3
Newline DELETE ops (lines being joined)
.IP 4. 3
Newline INSERT ops (lines being split)
.RE
.PP
Keeps and \\n ops stay in place as anchors/boundaries.
.PP
This layer also applies cross-hunk line_offset (cumulative \\n_ins - \\n_del from prior hunks) so positions are correct across the entire file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to /tmp/ad_debug/.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
V2 TSV format (see
.BR ad (1)
for the format specification).
.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. This layer has no user-configurable options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_layer_reorder < raw_ops.txt > reordered_ops.txt
Reorder ops and set positions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_compute (1),
.BR ad (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
\(em plugin contract documentation.
